{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, we found Harborview Supplies' invoice #4471 (October pallets). Our spam filter had held it in quarantine, and it is safe to release. A technician needs to approve the release, and we have requested that now. Once it is approved, the invoice will be delivered to your inbox. Your account is also locked after several failed sign-in attempts. We have requested an unlock, which a technician must approve. If you still can't sign in after that, please check whether an old password is saved on your phone or another device, since that can cause repeated lockouts. Please reply to confirm once the invoice shows up in your inbox.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user (Tom Becker, ID 4, Finance, locked, 5 failed logins, VPN enabled). Quarantine check found Q-1004 from billing@harborview-supplies.example, subject 'Invoice #4471 - October pallets', reason spam, releasable=true. Also Q-1005 (malware, scanner@docs-share.example) which must not be released. Queued release_email for Q-1004 (approval 1). Sign-in logs: 5 failed_password from corporate IP 203.0.113.10, with successful logins from the same IP and from residential VPN IP 198.51.100.24 that day, and no MFA denials, which points to a stale password rather than an attack. Queued unlock_account (approval 2). Technician should confirm the sender domain is the known Harborview vendor before approving. No KB article covers this exact case; KB-007 was followed for the quarantine release. Neither approval has run yet.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-007"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
